 from the mushrooms and chop them up to add to the sauce. Make 4 balls of mild Italian sausage, place one into each mushroom cap and flatten it out like a hamburger. Place the stuffed mushrooms in a shallow baking dish with enough water to cover the bottom of the dish 1/4 inch deep then into the oven preheated to 350 degrees.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"orfe15335","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-o8np","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"pn2gf5336","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-5n5ta","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Make the Marinara","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"ozcs05338","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-rgf6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Add the onions to a sauce pan with a tablespoon of olive oil and saute' them until they are translucent. Now add the garlic for just a minute or two then stir in the rest of the ingredients. I add the chopped mushrooms last so they wouldn't cook down too much and still retain some of their texture. Bring the pot to a low boil then reduce the heat to low and let it simmer for twenty minutes or so. Add the truffle or mushroom oil now if using.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foregro